\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} Introduction}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $}
 Introduction}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 K} introduction}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 +{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 +} 00000}} Introduction
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par Calmira is a complete 16-bit shell that lets you manage files, launch applications and control tasks.  It brings Windows 3.1 up to date with some of the advanced user interface enhancements from the Windows world, and for most people, provides welcome rel
ief from the awkwardness of File Manager.
\par 
\par \pard \s5\qc \{bmc intro1.bmp\}
\par \pard \s5 
\par The installation is simple -- just copy a few files into a directory, and you are ready to go.  If you have used the Windows 95 interface before, you should feel quite at home, but in any case, it won't take long to get used to the new look and feel.

\par 
\par \pard \s5\qc \{bmc intro2.bmp\}
\par \pard \s5 
\par There many settings and options which you can customise, and if that's not enough, then you can even re-write it (or get someone to do it for you!). Calmira is free and the source code is included in this package.  You are free to modify and redistribute 
it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} Changes}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $}
 What's new in Calmira 2.0}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 K} whats new}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 +{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 +} 00000}}
 What's new in Calmira 2.0
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par Here are some of the new features and changes since the last version, Calmira Source Release 1.0.  Hundreds of changes have been made, and the following list only contains some of the most important improvements.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Icon windows and Explorer
\par \pard\plain \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Windows can have better dimensions (2x2, 3x3...)}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Status bar can change to one-panel layout for narrow windows}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Title bar can display just the folder name without the path}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Full pathnames appear in popup hints over the }{\f2 status bar}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Miniature icons in list view, and new small icons view}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  List view can display only the columns you need to see}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Multiple file specifications can be used for the filter}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Explorer automatically moves and resizes associated windows}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Option to capitalise the first character of each filename}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Registered files can have their extension hidden}{\f2 \line }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Folders can be deleted from the tree view}{\f2 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 \{bmc b.bmp\} You can print a file by dragging it to the Print Manager window
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 File management
\par \pard\plain \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  File association facilities in File Properties dialog box}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  File processing can be interrupted while copying a file}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  The Find, Run and Start Properties dialogs can be resized}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Drag-and-drop can be configured to move files by default}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  The Run dialog can be set to close automatically}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Right mouse button can be used for fast file opening}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Bin op}{\f2 erations use progress box }{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Objects can be moved to the bin when deleted.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Description files are merged when directories are merged}{\f2 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 \{bmc b.bmp\} Open With feature is available in the Find Dialog
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Aliases can have a user-defined extension
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Shortcuts and aliases
\par \pard\plain \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\f2 \{}{\f2 bmc b.bmp}{\f2 \}}{\f2  Shortcuts can be created from the desktop}{\f2 
