\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Installation
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Copy all the files into a single directory of your hard disk, for example, c:\\Calmira.  Avoid putting these in your Windows directory.
\par 
\par The INI files are constantly modified, so the directory must have write permissions.  If you are using it over a network, you can make Calmira load its settings from the Windows directory.  See the {\uldb Miscellaneous Settings}{\v MiscSettings}
 topic for details.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 3D controls library
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Calmira requires the Ctl3dv2.dll module which is supplied in a ZIP file.  If you don't already have this file in your \\Windows\\
System directory, unzip it to there.  Do not leave Ctl3dv2.dll in the same directory as Calmira.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Setting Calmira as the shell
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
If you don't need Program Manager any more, you can use Calmira as the Windows shell.  You need to modify the System.ini file in your Windows directory, so make a backup copy of it first.  Look for the [Boot] section, where you will find something like:

\par 
\par {\f5 [Boot]}{\f5 
\par }{\f5 shell=progman.exe}{\f5 
\par }
\par Comment this out by adding a semi-colon in front of it, and add a line pointing to Calmira, for example
\par 
\par {\f5 [Boot]}{\f5 
\par }{\f5 ;shell=progman.exe}{\f5 
\par }{\f5 shell=c:}{\f5 \\}{\f5 calmira}{\f5 \\}{\f5 calmira.exe}{\f5 
\par }
\par Restart Windows for the new shell to take effect.  If you encounter problems when loading Windows, reset the shell to Program Manager and see the {\uldb Common Problems}{\v CommonProbs} section for more help.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Uninstalling
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Simply delete all the files in the Calmira directory.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} Upgrading}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $}
 Upgrading from Calmira 1.0}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 K} upgrading; files; icons; whats new; calmira.ini; start.ini; settings; options}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 +{\footnote 
\pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 +} 00000}} Upgrading from Calmira 1.0
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Replacing files
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 You should replace all the Calmira 1.0 files, {\i except} your Start.ini file.  It is important that you replace Calmira.ini because it contains new sections which are required for Calmira 2.0 to work correctly.  
\par 
\par You can, if you wish, copy the shortcut sections across and set the NumShorts property in the [Desktop] sections accordingly.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Object names
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 The "System Window" has been renamed "Computer" and the "System Tray" has been renamed "Applet Tray".
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Icons
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
Several new icons have been added, and because they are sorted by name, their positions in the file are now different.  So if your shortcuts or Start Menu items specified an icon index, some of these may need to be modified to show the correct icon again.

\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Option changes
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Several unnecessary settings have been removed, for example, the option to copy files in the background.  Calmi
ra is permanently configured to use the more powerful settings. Options have only been removed when it is certain that performance on slower computers will not be affected.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} QuickTour}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $} Quick Tour}}
 {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 K} quick tour}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 +{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 +} 00000}} Quick Tour
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par Here are the major components of Calmira -- click on a graphic to jump to the desired topic.  Remember that you can get context sensitive help at any time by pressing F1, and right clicking on many objects will pop up a context sensitive menu.  Explore, a
nd have fun...
\par 
