Use a suitable video driver.  Using a display driver with a high resolution or large number of colours results in slower display performance.  Calmira is graphics intensive, and you are recommended to use a 16 colour VGA driver or 256 colour generic Super
}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057  VGA driver from Microsoft. }{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
\par }{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
\par }{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 \{}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 bmc b.bmp}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 \}}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 \tab }{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
Look for the latest video and sound driver upgrades from the original hardware manufacturers, or from Microsoft.}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
