y not to load drivers that are not needed.  Look in Control Panel to see what you've accumulated over the years...}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
\par }{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
\par }{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 \{}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 bmc b.bmp}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 \}}{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 \tab }{\plain \f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
If you run an application that seems to use up system resources or memory every time it runs, try to keep it open instead of closing and reopening it many times. }
\par \pard\plain \s5\fi-270\li270\tx270 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab Check your screen savers to make sure that they are not overusing resources.
\par 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab Look at the Taskbar's memory and resource indicators regularly.  If some programs appear to be using large amounts, try not to run them together.  
\par 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab If you suspect that RAM or resources are being leaked by some programs, use Calmira's "Restart Windows" facility frequently to reclaim them.
\par 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab Look through all of your PIF files to make sure that their memory requirements have been set to the lowest possible values.  Programs which only use DPMI memory (Dos Protected Mode Interface) do not need any EMS or XMS memory.
\par \pard \s5 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Performance tips for 386 Enhanced Mode
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard \s5\fi-270\li270\tx270 \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab Use a permanent swap file rather than a temporary one.
\par 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab Enable 32-bit disk access and 32-bit file access if available.
\par 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab 
If you have a Super VGA graphics card, use the MonoUmb.386 device driver that is included in MS-DOS, which allows Windows to use the monochrome memory region for running programs.  For full details, see the Readme.txt file in your DOS directory.
\par 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab Turn off graphics port trapping for PIF files to speed up DOS programs.  Edit the PIF file's Advanced section and uncheck the port monitors (Text, Low Graphics and High Graphics).
\par 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\}\tab Turn off FileSysChange setting in the [386Enh] section of System.ini to speed up DOS programs.  The feature allows File Manager to detect disk changes made by DOS applications, but this isn't used when you run Calmira.
\par \pard \s5 
\par 
